    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0339" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/3036: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-23T20:00:00-04:00">May 23, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>292. For Briggs from Walmsley. Your 313 and 320, May 14 and 18.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d348-f1"/> I understand the BEW<anchor n="3" xml:id="d348-f2"/> has
                    written the DSC approving the proposed delivery of up to 10,000,000 gallons of
                    this year’s blackstrap production after January 1, 1943, according to the
                    formula suggested in your 320. I expect that the DSC would like to write <pb
                        facs="0340" n="326" xml:id="pg326"/> in a latest delivery date, say about
                    February 15, 1943. I further expect a letter from Goodloe<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d348-f3"/> Monday on the basis of which I shall telephone you; but
                    in the meantime Sabin<anchor n="5" xml:id="d348-f4"/> assures me the DSC will be
                    pleased to hear from the Institute on the subject.</p>
                <p>The DSC’s acquiescence is neither a commitment nor a guide with regard to next
                    year’s blackstrap price; so please dispel any optimistic assumption which may be
                    made in this regard. [Walmsley.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d348-f1" n="2" xml:id="d348-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 313, May 14, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d348-f2" n="3" xml:id="d348-f2-content">
                <p>Board of Economic Warfare.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d348-f3" n="4" xml:id="d348-f3-content">
                <p>John D. Goodloe, executive vice president of the Defense Supplies
                    Corporation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d348-f4" n="5" xml:id="d348-f4-content">
                <p>S. H. Sabin, a vice president of the Defense Supplies Corporation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
